>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `LINARITH_TAC`

``` hol4
linarithLib.LINARITH_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Proves a goal using full linear-arithmetic preprocessing and certificate
replay.

`LINARITH_TAC thms` is
`CFG_LINARITH_TAC linarithLib.default_config thms`. It inserts persistent
`[arith]` facts and each unmarked theorem in `thms`, negates the
conclusion, filters irrelevant assumptions, and converts what remains to
negation normal form, decomposing conjunctions and existentials into
separate assumptions.

It then searches. At each step it tries to refute the constraints in
hand; only if that fails does it take a single case split and continue on
both cases. A case split eliminates a disjunctive assumption where there
is one, and otherwise applies an operator-splitting rule. Where neither
applies it adds the facts registered instances supply for the atoms it
finds — division, modulus, and `Num` facts for the shipped instances —
and tries to refute once more before giving up.

Case splits are therefore taken on demand rather than expanded in
advance, and a goal costs the cases its arithmetic actually needs rather
than the size of its disjunctive normal form. The disjunctive assumption
split is the one with the fewest disjuncts still consistent with the
literals already assumed, so a disjunction whose other cases are already
refuted costs one branch rather than two.

The split corpus consists of persistent `[arith_split]` declarations,
per-instance rules, and arguments marked `markerLib.Split th`. Classical,
simplifier, and Iff markers are rejected. The default `neq_limit` and
`split_limit` are both 9. The tactic has close-or-fail semantics.

### Failure

Fails if preprocessing or linear arithmetic does not close every goal, if
a needed carrier has no registered instance, if a limit is exceeded, or
if an argument has an unsupported marker. A malformed split theorem is
also rejected.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem linarith_tac_example:
  !m n : num. MIN m n <= m
Proof
  rpt strip_tac >>
  linarithLib.LINARITH_TAC []
QED
```

